[start-outcomes] After this part you should be able to
1. tell a braced frame from an unbraced one, and name the sub-frame the course uses for the beams of a floor, for one beam and for a column;
2. arrange the variable load for the largest sagging and hogging moments, by Load Set 1 of EC2 and Load Set 2 of the Malaysian National Annex;
3. work out the load on a frame beam from the slab panels on either side with Table 3.15;
4. analyse the beams of a floor as a continuous beam by moment distribution, and find the shears, the span moments and the envelope;
5. find the column moments by the one-free-joint sub-frame, and the moment the beam carries at an end support.
